  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Given the circle \\(x^2+y^2=25\\) and the line \\(x=3\\), what is the chord length?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The distance from the center to the chord is 3. Half the chord length is \\(\\sqrt{25-9}=4\\), so the chord length is 8.\n\nAlternative method 1: Find the chord endpoints\n\nThe chord lies on the vertical line \\(x=3\\), so find its endpoints by substituting into the circle equation:\n\\[\ny^2=25-3^2=16.\n\\]\nThe two solutions are \\(y=4\\) and \\(y=-4\\), so the endpoints are \\((3,4)\\) and \\((3,-4)\\). Their vertical separation is \\(4-(-4)=8\\). Therefore the chord length is \\(8\\).",
